<title>GERMANY: Hoechst says no decision yet on sick pay.</title>
<headline>Hoechst says no decision yet on sick pay.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals and pharmaceuticals group Hoechst AG said on Wednesday that it has not yet decided whether to cut sick pay allowances under a new German law.</p>
<p>&quot;We are discussing whether to implement the new law,&quot; a Hoechst spokesman told Reuters in answer to a query.</p>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG and BASF AG have both announced they will cut sick pay benefits to 80 percent on October 1 under the law approved by German parliament.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
